+We develop residual error bounds for neural and reduced approximations of
+European-put pricing trajectories under the Carr--Geman--Madan--Yor model.
+A Crank--Nicolson energy estimate combines the initial discrepancy with an
+accumulated dual residual norm in the constrained spline space. A two-sided
+Riesz bracket supplies an upper bound even when iterative solves are
+incomplete, enabling tolerance-controlled acceptance and correction.
+The guarantees concern the assembled discrete problem in exact arithmetic;
+the implementation is evaluated in ordinary floating point.
+Matched benchmarks show that the neural workflow is slower than an
+optimised direct solve, whereas a mass-weighted POD approximation achieves
+direct acceptance and lower online cost. Assembly and certification dominate
+the optimised solver costs. Independent Fourier prices and refinement
+studies distinguish the certified surrogate error from spatial, temporal
+and domain errors. The resulting framework provides scheme-consistent
+certification and a quantitative account of its computational value.
