-above solo medians. Query pairing limits but does not eliminate this
-contention effect. The bootstrap intervals below describe variation over
-queries within these runs, not uncertainty from hardware contention or
-other machines. A time ratio is
-$t_{\rm method}/t_{\rm baseline}$ per query (values below one are faster),
-summarised by its geometric mean over the queries on which both methods are
-verified, with a 95\% bootstrap interval over queries and the coverage of
-each method.
